---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';

const credits = [
  { name: 'heic-decode', license: 'ISC', url: 'https://github.com/catdad-experiments/heic-decode' },
  { name: 'libheif-js', license: 'LGPL-3.0', url: 'https://github.com/catdad-experiments/libheif-js' },
  { name: 'libheif', license: 'LGPL-3.0', url: 'https://github.com/strukturag/libheif' },
  { name: 'fflate', license: 'MIT', url: 'https://github.com/101arrowz/fflate' },
];
---

<Base
  title={`How ${site.name} keeps your files private`}
  description={`${site.name} processes images entirely in your browser. Here's how it works and how to verify that nothing is uploaded.`}
>
  <article class="container prose">
    <h1>How {site.name} works</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      {site.name} converts, compresses, and resizes photos entirely in your browser. Your files are never uploaded,
      stored, or seen by anyone.
    </p>

    <h2>What happens to your file</h2>
    <p>
      When you choose a photo, your browser reads it from your disk into memory. The tool decodes it right there,
      resizes and re-encodes it with the canvas API (and a HEIC decoder for iPhone photos), and hands the result back
      as a download. When you close the tab, it's gone.
    </p>

    <h2>How to check for yourself</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Go offline.</strong> Load the convert page, turn off your wifi, then use the tool. It keeps working
        because it never needed a server.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Watch the network.</strong> Open your browser's developer tools, go to the Network tab, and process a
        file. You'll see no request carrying your photo.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Read the security policy.</strong> Every page sends a Content-Security-Policy that only allows
        connections back to this site, plus cookieless visit counting. Your browser enforces it even if the code tried
        to send your file elsewhere.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We count page visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which uses no cookies and doesn't track you across sites. It
      never sees your files.
    </p>

    <h2>Open source</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is free software under the MIT license. The HEIC decoder is
      <a href="https://github.com/strukturag/libheif" rel="noopener">libheif</a>, used as a WebAssembly module under
      LGPL-3.0. The full source code is at
      <a href={site.sourceUrl} rel="noopener">{site.sourceUrl.replace('https://', '')}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>It is built on these open-source projects:</p>
    <ul>
      {
        credits.map((credit) => (
          <li>
            <a href={credit.url} rel="noopener">
              {credit.name}
            </a>{' '}
            ({credit.license})
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <p>Made by <a href={site.studioUrl} rel="noopener">{site.studio}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
